Personally, I think the problem with graphical dungeon games is that
they can easily take way too long to animate.  In Nethack, we have the
option of using shift+arrow keys to run all the way across a dungeon
level within a couple of seconds.  Compare this to a graphical dungeon
game (i.e. Eye of the Beholder), where it literally takes a full
second to move 1 square in the dungeon, which means running across a
single dungeon level literally takes about 5-10 minutes, even if it is
completely explored and completely devoid of monsters.

A very extreme example is the newer graphical dungeon game, Temple of
Elemental Evil.  One single turn can easily take 30 seconds to play,
where you take about 5 seconds deciding what to do, and 25 seconds
watching the pretty game animations.



